menu "ha_gatt_exec"

config HA_GATT_ALLOW_WRITE
    bool "Allow arbitrary GATT writes (actuation)"
    default n
    help
        Arbitrary GATT characteristic writes are an ACTUATION primitive: a validly-signed command
        could otherwise drive any BLE device's characteristics. A telemetry-only relay never needs
        them (sub/read/collect suffice; the CCCD notify-enable in a "sub" step is not arbitrary
        actuation). Least privilege: leave this OFF (n) so the write path is not even compiled into
        the image. Set it to y ONLY in a per-actuator firmware build's sdkconfig.defaults.

endmenu
